A||||5||hutch84fierose||How do you remove the trim???????||||1||
Z||000000||hutch84fierose||07-21-2001||01:51 PM||||I am plan on removing the trim on my 84 fiero and painting it to make it look better and brighten it up but I was wonderin the proper way to remove it withoug damaging anything else thanks jon||||reg||1
Z||000001||California Kid||07-21-2001||02:50 PM||||Buy a "Chilton" Repair Manual for your car from local parts dealer. Once you know where all the fasteners and types of fasteners are located, it's a piece of cake !!! Just make sure you don't start pulling to hard on items, as they have become brittle with age.||||reg||6
Z||000002||Standard||07-21-2001||08:01 PM||||Really big hammer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  just gotta know where to hit it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Most of the trim is held on by these annoying little clips that will break no matter how careful you are not to break them.. so gather up a bunch of extra ones before you get started to save on the frustration later.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||07-21-2001||08:15 PM||||take out visible torx screws. the clips r supposed to come off by pushing the molding up, and while doing that pry out the top. Just hope there all still flexible enough to not break.||||reg||1
Z||000004||AusFiero||07-22-2001||03:07 AM||||I heard in 84's you can just burn it out   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Only kiddin. don't know why Fieros have such a bad rap for it. Dozens of makes in the world have suffered the same fate. Some of them very expensive Euro models included.<BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A><p>[This message has been edited by AusFiero (edited 07-22-2001).]||202.139.20.3||reg||1
